  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Deepak vs The State Of M.P. on 23 March, 2026 Neutral Citation No. 2026:Mphc-Jbp:26134 1 In The High Court Of Madhya Pradesh At Jabalpur Before Hon'Ble Shri Justice Himanshu Joshi On The 23rd Of March, 2026 Misc. Criminal Case No. 17331 of 2023 Deepak Versus The State Of M.P. Appearance: Dr. Anuvad Shrivastava - Advocate for the applicant. Smt. Chetna Gupta - Pl for the respondent/State . Order",
    "facts": "2. The relevant facts are that a complaint was filed under Section 26(2)(1) read with Section 59 of the Food Safety and Standards Act, 2006 against one Virendra Kumar Jain, proprietor of \"Virendra Pan Masala\", alleging sale of sub-standard pan masala. 3. Initially, the present applicant was not arraigned as an accused in the case. Subsequently, an application under Section 319 of the Code of NEUTRAL CITATION NO. 2026:MPHC-JBP:26134 2 MCRC-17331-2023 Criminal Procedure was filed seeking to implead the applicant as an accused. The said application was rejected by the Judicial Magistrate First Class (JMFC) vide order dated 19.02.2015. However, in revision, the said order was [LEAKAGE_MASK] and the application was allowed on 27.08.2015. 4. The applicant thereafter filed an application (Annexure A/5) before the trial Court seeking discharge, and prosecution of the nominated person (Mr. Pankaj P.Wala), appointed by Board Resolution dated 05.03.2012 under Section 66 of the Act. Hence, the present petition.",
    "arguments": "6. Learned counsel for the applicant contends that Section 66 of the Act provides a statutory mechanism for nomination, and liability must fall on the nominated person. The company had already nominated a responsible person for food safety compliance. The applicant is merely a Director and not in charge of day-to-day operations. Continuation of proceedings against the applicant amounts to abuse of process of law. 7. Learned counsel for the State/respondent submits that the NEUTRAL CITATION NO. 2026:MPHC-JBP:26134 3 MCRC-17331-2023 applicant has already been impleaded as an accused pursuant to earlier orders upheld by the High Court. The issue of liability cannot be adjudicated at this stage. 9. Section 66 of the Food Safety and Standards Act. 2006 provides that where an offence is committed by a company the persons in charge are liable, and the company may nominate a responsible person for a unit/branch.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "6. Learned counsel for the applicant contends that Section 66 of the Act provides a statutory mechanism for nomination, and liability must fall on the nominated person. The company had already nominated a responsible person for food safety compliance. The applicant is merely a Director and not in charge of day-to-day operations. Continuation of proceedings against the applicant amounts to abuse of process of law. 7. Learned counsel for the State/respondent submits that the NEUTRAL CITATION NO. 2026:MPHC-JBP:26134 3 MCRC-17331-2023 applicant has already been impleaded as an accused pursuant to earlier orders upheld by the High Court.",
    "respondent_arguments": "The issue of liability cannot be adjudicated at this stage.",
    "other_lawyer_arguments": "9. Section 66 of the Food Safety and Standards Act. 2006 provides that where an offence is committed by a company the persons in charge are liable, and the company may nominate a responsible person for a unit/branch."
  },
